**Definition 8.2 (operational meaning of the missing law).** Interpret
(RB.43) through the existing FC Theorem 8.1 and GC Propositions
10.1 and 12.2, applied to that very law after compatible merging:
all eight moments, physical capacity, $K=r$ and
$J_t=y\cdot B-\lambda r$ must hold simultaneously. Their original
height and minimum-count dictionary is

$$
\mathcal T(s,t)=\frac{H_0+y\cdot B(t)-\lambda r}{2},\qquad
n_{\rm tot}(s,t)=1+n_t(r).
\tag{RB.44}
$$

Here $s=s_0r/\sqrt\alpha$, $H_0$ is the fixed positive high height,
and GC.10 is an identity of minima. A law satisfying (RB.43) would
therefore have a realization with at most seven supported low labels
and one counted coherent high, with all the quantum and entire-fibre
requirements of Assumption 1.1. Coefficient weights, failure
intensities, endpoint nodes, matrix rank, hidden Kraus indices and
actual acquisition labels are distinct quantities. Theorem 7.1
provides no representation satisfying (RB.43).

